.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-piv-derive 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-piv\-derive \- Derive a raw ECDH/X25519 shared secret with a slot\*(Aqs key (no KDF)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-piv\-derive\fR [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-pin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISLOT\fR> <\fIPEER_PUBLIC_KEY\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Derive a raw ECDH/X25519 shared secret with a slot\*(Aqs key (no KDF)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-pin\fR \fI<PIN>\fR
PIN code (prompted when needed)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISLOT\fR>
PIV slot holding an ECC/X25519 key
.TP
<\fIPEER_PUBLIC_KEY\fR>
File containing the peer public key (uncompressed SEC1 point, or 32 bytes for X25519) (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdin)
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>
File to write the shared secret to (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdout)
